# MIDAS database migrations (Alembic)

Schema changes are managed with Alembic from this directory. SQLAlchemy models in `../backend/app/db/models.py` remain the source of truth; generate revisions from model diffs.

## Prerequisites

Embedded Postgres must be running:

```powershell
cd database
uv run midas-db start
```

## Common commands

```powershell
cd database

# Apply all pending migrations
uv run alembic upgrade head

# Create a new migration after editing backend models
uv run alembic revision --autogenerate -m "describe your change"

# Show current revision
uv run alembic current

# Roll back one revision
uv run alembic downgrade -1
```

`midas-db init` runs migrations automatically after starting embedded Postgres.

## DBeaver

After `midas-db start` or `init`, the DBeaver connection **MIDAS (embedded)** is updated automatically from `.midas/database.json`. To refresh manually:

```powershell
uv run midas-dbeaver
```

Embedded Postgres uses trust authentication — connect as user `postgres` with an empty password. Restart DBeaver if the port changed.
